<title>UK: Granada declines comment on Man Utd report.</title>
<headline>Granada declines comment on Man Utd report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Granada Group Plc on Friday declined comment on a report in the Times that it had expressed an interest in acquiring soccer club Manchester United Plc, citing a policy not to respond to market speculation.</p>
<p>&quot;We can't comment,&quot; said a spokeswoman for the media and hotels group.  </p>
<p>Earlier, Manchester United shares rocketed after the Times said a number of companies including Granada and Whitbread had both expressed an interest in buying the club.</p>
<p>However, it is understood that Granada has no plans to make a bid for United and is still busy in the wake of its acquisition of hotels group Forte earlier this year.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
